Use the design Skill's selection guide to choose a workflow shape. Read only the pattern references relevant to your choice, then read the public API pages you need. The catalog is a vocabulary, not a whitelist: you may combine or adapt patterns when the task justifies it.

Your SEARCH_TYPE is a plain child Search. Subclass `engine.search.Search`, implement undecorated `explore()`, omit `kind`, and return `SearchOutput` from `engine.builtin.aibuildai`. Do not subclass `AIBuildAISearch`.

Start with Agent for authored work. Use Program only when all four statements are true: every execution step is settled before launch; the Output can be classified by code; the Program Action does not diagnose an open problem or make a new plan; and a separate resource, retry, cancellation, or parallel boundary has real value. If any statement is uncertain, use Agent. Program runs a settled plan and handles its fixed terminal result. Agent decides the plan and what to do when the facts require judgment or a changed plan.

An Agent may use short Python or shell commands while it investigates. Code use alone does not justify a Program. Do not make an Agent wait for or repeat a settled long process; give that process a Program boundary when all four statements are true.

Choose names that state the task, algorithm, or role. Do this for every Search, Input, Output, Agent, Composite, and Program. A Composite class's name is also its node name: every invocation appears in the run log, the workspace path, and the Web graph as that name's snake_case plus a number, so `class TrainAndScore(Composite[Input])` runs as `train_and_score_1`, `train_and_score_2`, while a class named `RunStage` or `Step` leaves every reader guessing what the node does. In `search/__init__.py`, import the actual top-level Search class and export it as `SEARCH_TYPE`. The export name is fixed. The class name is not fixed.

Write the package under search/. The loader accepts any valid package layout. Put authored Program classes under `programs/` and authored Composite classes under `composites/`. Use this standard layout:

```
search/
├── __init__.py          exports SEARCH_TYPE
├── search.py            the Search class
├── io.py                its Input and Output types
├── agents/              your own Agent classes, if any
├── composites/          your own Composite classes, if any
├── programs/            your own Program classes, if any
└── prompts/agent/*.j2   the prompt each of your Agents renders
```

